IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part7-powers`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 7, the sections and subsections pass 1 left unencoded (pass 2).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Pass 1 encoded only the provisions of Part 7 that fix a deadline or a limit of time, and left the rest
-- "inert" as rules of construction, as widening an official's power, or as addressed to an official. None of those is a ground for
-- leaving a provision out. Each provision below says something a person can test, and is encoded as a gate: a rule that returns
-- JUST the answer the provision gives when its conditions are met, and NOTHING when the provision says nothing about the case.
-- Where the provision turns on a judgment, the judgment is an INPUT. The rules pass 1 encoded for ss 33(4)(b), 33A(1)(ba) and (c),
-- 33AB, 34A, 34B(1) and 34C are in au-part7-powers.l4 and are not repeated.

§ `Part 7: Powers, functions and duties (the provisions that complete ss 33 to 34C)`

§§ `Section 33(1): powers, functions and duties are exercised from time to time`

DECLARE `What an Act confers` IS ONE OF
    `a power`
    `a function`
    `a duty`

DECLARE `What section 33(1) says is to be done` IS ONE OF
    `the power may be exercised`
    `the function must be performed`
    `the duty must be performed`
    `section 33(1) says nothing about it`

-- src:626 | (1) Where an Act confers a power or function or imposes a duty, then the power may be exercised and the function or duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(1) (src:626)
GIVEN conferred IS A `What an Act confers`
      `the occasion requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What section 33(1) says is to be done`
`what section 33(1) says is to be done` conferred `the occasion requires it` MEANS
    IF `the occasion requires it`
    THEN CONSIDER conferred
         WHEN `a power` THEN `the power may be exercised`
         WHEN `a function` THEN `the function must be performed`
         WHEN `a duty` THEN `the duty must be performed`
    ELSE `section 33(1) says nothing about it`

§§ `Section 33(2A): the word may`

-- The date the subsection commenced is not in the text (fork F19, NOTES.md), so whether the Act was assented to after it is an INPUT.
-- src:628 | (2A) Where an Act assented to after the commencement of this subsection provides that a person, court or body may do a particular act or thing, and the word “may” is used, the act or thing may be done at the discretion of the person, court or body.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(2A) (src:628)
GIVEN `the Act was assented to after the commencement of subsection 33(2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act provides that a person, court or body may do a particular act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word may is used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the act or thing may be done at the discretion of the person, court or body` `the Act was assented to after the commencement of subsection 33(2A)` `the Act provides that a person, court or body may do a particular act or thing` `the word may is used` MEANS
    IF `the Act was assented to after the commencement of subsection 33(2A)` AND `the Act provides that a person, court or body may do a particular act or thing` AND `the word may is used`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 33(2B): vacancies in the membership of a body`

-- src:630 | (2B) Where an Act confers a power or function, or imposes a duty, on a body, whether incorporated or unincorporated, the exercise of the power or the performance of the function or duty is not affected merely because of a vacancy or vacancies in the membership of the body.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(2B) (src:630)
GIVEN `the Act confers a power or function, or imposes a duty, on a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason offered is a vacancy or vacancies in the membership of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the exercise or performance is affected merely because of a vacancy in the membership` `the Act confers a power or function, or imposes a duty, on a body` `the body is incorporated` `the reason offered is a vacancy or vacancies in the membership of the body` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers a power or function, or imposes a duty, on a body` AND `the reason offered is a vacancy or vacancies in the membership of the body`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 33(3) and (3AA): power to make an instrument includes power to repeal, amend and vary it`

DECLARE `Thing done to an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `to repeal it`
    `to rescind it`
    `to revoke it`
    `to amend it`
    `to vary it`
    `to do something else to it`

DECLARE `Condition that governs the later act` IS ONE OF
    `the like condition`
    `the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied`

-- src:632 | (3) Where an Act confers a power to make, grant or issue any instrument of a legislative or administrative character (including rules, regulations or by-laws) the power shall be construed as including a power exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like conditions (if any) to repeal, rescind, revoke, amend, or vary any such instrument.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(3) (src:632)
GIVEN `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `Thing done to an instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to make the instrument includes the power to do this to it` `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` thing MEANS
    IF `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `to repeal it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to rescind it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to amend it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to vary it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to do something else to it` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 3AA: a condition that must be satisfied before the making and can stop being satisfied afterwards is an "ongoing condition". For a
-- repeal, rescission or revocation, the "like conditions" are replaced, to that extent, by the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied.
-- For an amendment or variation, 3AA says nothing, so subsection (3)'s like conditions stand.
-- src:633 | (3AA) If a condition (the ongoing condition):
-- src:634 | (a) must be satisfied before the making, granting or issuing of an instrument; and
-- src:635 | (b) is capable of ceasing to be satisfied after the making, granting or issuing of the instrument;
-- src:636 | subsection (3) has effect, in relation to the repeal, rescission or revocation of the instrument, as if the reference to like conditions (to the extent that the reference relates to the ongoing condition) were a reference to the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied.
-- src:637 | Example: A Minister may give a person a written permission if, among other things, the Minister is satisfied the person is of good character.
-- src:638 | This condition is capable of ceasing to be satisfied after the giving of the permission.
-- src:639 | The Minister may repeal, rescind or revoke the permission in the like manner if the Minister ceases to be satisfied that the person is of good character.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(3AA) (src:633-639)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing done to an instrument`
      `the condition must be satisfied before the making, granting or issuing of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is capable of ceasing to be satisfied after the making, granting or issuing of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Condition that governs the later act`
`the condition that governs doing this to the instrument` thing `the condition must be satisfied before the making, granting or issuing of the instrument` `the condition is capable of ceasing to be satisfied after the making, granting or issuing of the instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `to repeal it` THEN JUST ongoingOrLike
    WHEN `to rescind it` THEN JUST ongoingOrLike
    WHEN `to revoke it` THEN JUST ongoingOrLike
    WHEN `to amend it` THEN JUST `the like condition`
    WHEN `to vary it` THEN JUST `the like condition`
    WHEN `to do something else to it` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        ongoingOrLike MEANS
            IF `the condition must be satisfied before the making, granting or issuing of the instrument` AND `the condition is capable of ceasing to be satisfied after the making, granting or issuing of the instrument`
            THEN `the ongoing condition ceasing to be satisfied`
            ELSE `the like condition`

§§ `Section 33(3A), (3AB), (3AC) and (3B): the scope of a power to make an instrument`

DECLARE `Way of making an instrument as to matters` IS ONE OF
    `with respect to some only of the matters`
    `with respect to a particular class of the matters`
    `with respect to particular classes of the matters`
    `making different provision with respect to different matters`
    `making different provision with respect to different classes of matters`
    `in some other way as to matters`

DECLARE `Candidate for a matter` IS ONE OF
    `a thing that is a matter`
    `a person that is a matter`
    `an animal that is a matter`
    `something else that is a matter`
    `something that is not a matter`

-- src:641 | (3A) Where an Act confers a power to make, grant or issue any instrument of a legislative or administrative character (including rules, regulations or by-laws) with respect to particular matters (however the matters are described), the power shall be construed as including a power to make, grant or issue such an instrument with respect to some only of those matters or with respect to a particular class or particular classes of those matters and to make different provision with respect to different matters or different classes of matters.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(3A) (src:641)
GIVEN `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character with respect to particular matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way of making an instrument as to matters`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power includes making the instrument in this way` `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character with respect to particular matters` way MEANS
    IF `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character with respect to particular matters`
    THEN CONSIDER way
         WHEN `with respect to some only of the matters` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `with respect to a particular class of the matters` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `with respect to particular classes of the matters` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `making different provision with respect to different matters` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `making different provision with respect to different classes of matters` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `in some other way as to matters` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:642 | (3AB) If an Act confers on a person or authority the power to make an instrument (except a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument or a rule of court):
-- src:643 | (a) specifying, declaring or prescribing a matter; or
-- src:644 | (b) doing anything in relation to a matter;
-- src:645 | then, in exercising the power, the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters.
-- src:646 | Note: This provision has a parallel, in relation to legislative instruments, and notifiable instruments, in section 13 of the Legislation Act 2003.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(3AB) (src:642-646)
GIVEN `the instrument is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a rule of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is to specify, declare or prescribe a matter, or to do anything in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person or authority may identify the matter by reference to a class or classes of matters` `the instrument is a legislative instrument` `the instrument is a notifiable instrument` `the instrument is a rule of court` `the power is to specify, declare or prescribe a matter, or to do anything in relation to a matter` MEANS
    IF   `the power is to specify, declare or prescribe a matter, or to do anything in relation to a matter`
         AND (NOT `the instrument is a legislative instrument`)
         AND (NOT `the instrument is a notifiable instrument`)
         AND (NOT `the instrument is a rule of court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:647 | (3AC) For the purposes of subsections (3A) and (3AB), matter includes thing, person and animal.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(3AC) (src:647)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for a matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a matter for subsections 33(3A) and 33(3AB)` candidate MEANS
    NOT (candidate EQUALS `something that is not a matter`)

-- src:648 | (3B) Where an Act confers a power to make, grant or issue any instrument of a legislative or administrative character (including rules, regulations or by-laws), the power shall not be taken, by implication, not to include the power to make provision for or in relation to a particular aspect of a matter by reason only that provision is made by the Act in relation to another aspect of that matter or in relation to another matter.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(3B) (src:648)
GIVEN `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason offered is that the Act makes provision in relation to another aspect of the matter or in relation to another matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power is taken, by implication, not to include power to make provision for a particular aspect of a matter` `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` `the only reason offered is that the Act makes provision in relation to another aspect of the matter or in relation to another matter` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` AND `the only reason offered is that the Act makes provision in relation to another aspect of the matter or in relation to another matter`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 33(4): a power to make appointments to an office or place`

DECLARE `What a power to make appointments includes` IS ONE OF
    `appointing a person to act in the office or place`
    `removing a person appointed`
    `suspending a person appointed`
    `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a person suspended`
    `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a sick or absent holder`
    `something else about appointments`

-- src:650 | (4) Where an Act confers upon any person or authority a power to make appointments to any office or place, the power shall be construed as including a power to appoint a person to act in the office or place until:
-- src:651 | (a) a person is appointed to the office or place; or
-- src:652 | (b) the expiration of 12 months after the office or place was created or became vacant, as the case requires;
-- src:653 | whichever first happens, and as also including a power to remove or suspend any person appointed, and to appoint another person temporarily in the place of any person so suspended or in place of any sick or absent holder of such office or place.
-- src:654 | Provided that where the power of such person or authority to make any such appointment is only exercisable upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of some other person or authority, such power to make an appointment to act in an office or place or such power of removal shall only be exercisable upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of such other person or authority.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(4) (src:650-654)
GIVEN `the Act confers on a person or authority a power to make appointments to an office or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `What a power to make appointments includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to make appointments includes this` `the Act confers on a person or authority a power to make appointments to an office or place` thing MEANS
    IF `the Act confers on a person or authority a power to make appointments to an office or place`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `appointing a person to act in the office or place` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `removing a person appointed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `suspending a person appointed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a person suspended` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a sick or absent holder` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `something else about appointments` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The proviso: where the power to make the appointment is only exercisable on a recommendation or with an approval or consent, the power
-- to appoint to act, and the power of removal, are exercisable only on that recommendation or with that approval or consent. The proviso
-- names those two powers and no others.
-- src:654 | Provided that where the power of such person or authority to make any such appointment is only exercisable upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of some other person or authority, such power to make an appointment to act in an office or place or such power of removal shall only be exercisable upon the recommendation or subject to the approval or consent of such other person or authority.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(4) proviso (src:654)
GIVEN thing IS A `What a power to make appointments includes`
      `the power to make the appointment is exercisable only on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of some other person or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power may be exercised as the proviso to section 33(4) requires` thing `the power to make the appointment is exercisable only on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of some other person or authority` `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given` MEANS
    IF `the power to make the appointment is exercisable only on the recommendation, or subject to the approval or consent, of some other person or authority`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `appointing a person to act in the office or place` THEN JUST `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given`
         WHEN `removing a person appointed` THEN JUST `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given`
         WHEN `suspending a person appointed` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a person suspended` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `appointing another person temporarily in the place of a sick or absent holder` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `something else about appointments` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 33(4)(a) and (b): the acting appointment lasts until the first of the two events. The 12-month event is the rule in
-- au-part7-powers.l4; the appointment event is an INPUT.
-- src:650 | (4) Where an Act confers upon any person or authority a power to make appointments to any office or place, the power shall be construed as including a power to appoint a person to act in the office or place until:
-- src:651 | (a) a person is appointed to the office or place; or
-- src:652 | (b) the expiration of 12 months after the office or place was created or became vacant, as the case requires;
-- src:653 | whichever first happens, and as also including a power to remove or suspend any person appointed, and to appoint another person temporarily in the place of any person so suspended or in place of any sick or absent holder of such office or place.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(4)(a) and (b) (src:650-653)
GIVEN `the day a person is appointed to the office or place, if one is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the acting appointment under section 33(4) ends` `the day a person is appointed to the office or place, if one is` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the 12 months for an acting appointment under section 33(4)` `the day the office or place was created or became vacant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST twelveMonths THEN
        CONSIDER `the day a person is appointed to the office or place, if one is`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST twelveMonths
        WHEN JUST appointed THEN JUST (IF appointed LESS THAN twelveMonths THEN appointed ELSE twelveMonths)

§§ `Section 33(5), 33AA: statutory declarations; reappointment`

-- src:656 | (5) Where an Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws) prescribing penalties not exceeding a specified amount or imprisonment for a specified period, that limitation on the penalties that may be prescribed does not prevent the instrument from requiring the making of a statutory declaration.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33(5) (src:656)
GIVEN `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument prescribing penalties not exceeding a specified amount or imprisonment for a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument requires the making of a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the limit on penalties prevents the instrument from requiring a statutory declaration` `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument prescribing penalties not exceeding a specified amount or imprisonment for a specified period` `the instrument requires the making of a statutory declaration` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers a power to make, grant or issue an instrument prescribing penalties not exceeding a specified amount or imprisonment for a specified period` AND `the instrument requires the making of a statutory declaration`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:657 | 33AA Power to appoint includes power to reappoint
-- src:658 | If an Act confers on a person or body a power to make an appointment, the power is taken to include a power of reappointment.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33AA (src:657-658)
GIVEN `the Act confers on a person or body a power to make an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to make the appointment includes a power of reappointment` `the Act confers on a person or body a power to make an appointment` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers on a person or body a power to make an appointment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 33A: acting in offices or positions (what pass 1 left)`

DECLARE `Thing the appointer may do under section 33A(1)` IS ONE OF
    `expressing the appointment to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment`
    `determining the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances`
    `terminating the appointment at any time`
    `something else about an acting appointment`

DECLARE `What the person acting has` IS ONE OF
    `all the powers of the holder of the office`
    `the functions and duties of the holder of the office`
    `the application of the Act concerned or any other Act as if the person were the holder`
    `something else the holder of the office has`

DECLARE `Ground for challenging a purported acting` IS ONE OF
    `the occasion to act had not arisen`
    `the occasion to act had ceased`
    `some other ground about acting`

-- src:667 | (1) Where a provision of an Act (other than subsection 33(4) of this Act) confers on a person or body (in this section called the appointer) a power to appoint a person (in this section called the appointee) to act in a particular office, then, except so far as the Act otherwise provides, the following paragraphs apply in relation to an appointment made under the provision:
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(1) (src:667)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of an Act other than subsection 33(4) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision confers on a person or body a power to appoint a person to act in a particular office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act otherwise provides about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 33A(1) applies to the appointment` `the provision is a provision of an Act other than subsection 33(4) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901` `the provision confers on a person or body a power to appoint a person to act in a particular office` `the Act otherwise provides about the matter` MEANS
        `the provision is a provision of an Act other than subsection 33(4) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901`
    AND `the provision confers on a person or body a power to appoint a person to act in a particular office`
    AND (NOT `the Act otherwise provides about the matter`)

-- src:667 | (1) Where a provision of an Act (other than subsection 33(4) of this Act) confers on a person or body (in this section called the appointer) a power to appoint a person (in this section called the appointee) to act in a particular office, then, except so far as the Act otherwise provides, the following paragraphs apply in relation to an appointment made under the provision:
-- src:668 | (a) the appointment may be expressed to have effect only in the circumstances specified in the instrument of appointment;
-- src:669 | (b) the appointer may:
-- src:670 | (i) determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances; and
-- src:671 | (ii) terminate the appointment at any time;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(1)(a) and (b) (src:667-671)
GIVEN `section 33A(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `Thing the appointer may do under section 33A(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointer may do this under section 33A(1)` `section 33A(1) applies` thing MEANS
    `section 33A(1) applies` AND (NOT (thing EQUALS `something else about an acting appointment`))

-- src:678 | (d) the appointment ceases to have effect if the appointee resigns in writing delivered to the appointer;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(1)(d) (src:678)
GIVEN `section 33A(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee resigns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resignation is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resignation is delivered to the appointer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointment ceases to have effect on the appointee's resignation` `section 33A(1) applies` `the appointee resigns` `the resignation is in writing` `the resignation is delivered to the appointer` MEANS
    `section 33A(1) applies` AND `the appointee resigns` AND `the resignation is in writing` AND `the resignation is delivered to the appointer`

-- src:679 | (e) while the appointee is acting in the office:
-- src:680 | (i) the appointee has and may exercise all the powers, and shall perform all the functions and duties, of the holder of the office; and
-- src:681 | (ii) that or any other Act applies in relation to the appointee as if the appointee were the holder of the office.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(1)(e) (src:679-681)
GIVEN `section 33A(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee is acting in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `What the person acting has`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has this while acting in the office` `section 33A(1) applies` `the appointee is acting in the office` thing MEANS
    `section 33A(1) applies` AND `the appointee is acting in the office` AND (NOT (thing EQUALS `something else the holder of the office has`))

-- src:683 | (2) If a provision of an Act provides for a person to act in a particular office (without the need for an appointment), then, except so far as the Act otherwise provides, while the person is acting in the office:
-- src:684 | (a) the person has and may exercise all the powers, and must perform all the functions and duties, of the holder of the office; and
-- src:685 | (b) the Act or any other Act applies in relation to the person as if the person were the holder of the office.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(2) (src:683-685)
GIVEN `the provision of an Act provides for a person to act in a particular office without the need for an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act otherwise provides about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is acting in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `What the person acting has`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person acting by operation of law has this while acting in the office` `the provision of an Act provides for a person to act in a particular office without the need for an appointment` `the Act otherwise provides about the matter` `the person is acting in the office` thing MEANS
        `the provision of an Act provides for a person to act in a particular office without the need for an appointment`
    AND (NOT `the Act otherwise provides about the matter`)
    AND `the person is acting in the office`
    AND (NOT (thing EQUALS `something else the holder of the office has`))

-- src:686 | (3) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act in the office mentioned in subsection (2) is not invalid merely because the occasion to act had not arisen or had ceased.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33A(3) (src:686)
GIVEN `the person purports to act in an office mentioned in subsection 33A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `Ground for challenging a purported acting`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the thing done is invalid merely because of this ground for purported acting` `the person purports to act in an office mentioned in subsection 33A(2)` ground MEANS
    IF `the person purports to act in an office mentioned in subsection 33A(2)`
    THEN CONSIDER ground
         WHEN `the occasion to act had not arisen` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `the occasion to act had ceased` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `some other ground about acting` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 33B: participation in meetings by telephone etc.`

DECLARE `Means of participating in a meeting` IS ONE OF
    `telephone`
    `closed-circuit television`
    `any other means of communication`

-- src:691 | (1) This section applies to a body (whether or not incorporated) established by an Act if the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33B(1) (src:691)
GIVEN `the body is established by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 33B applies to the body` `the body is established by an Act` `the body is incorporated` `the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held` MEANS
    `the body is established by an Act` AND `the Act requires or permits meetings of the members of the body to be held`

-- src:692 | (2) The body may permit its members to participate in a meeting, or all meetings, by:
-- src:693 | (a) telephone; or
-- src:694 | (b) closed-circuit television; or
-- src:695 | (c) any other means of communication.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33B(2) (src:692-695)
GIVEN `section 33B applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      means IS A `Means of participating in a meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body may permit its members to participate by this means` `section 33B applies` means MEANS
    `section 33B applies`

-- src:696 | (3) A member who participates in a meeting under a permission under subsection (2) is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum for the meeting.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33B(3) (src:696)
GIVEN `section 33B applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member participates in the meeting under the permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the member is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum` `section 33B applies` `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` `the member participates in the meeting under the permission` MEANS
    `section 33B applies` AND `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` AND `the member participates in the meeting under the permission`

-- src:697 | (4) The members of a body participating in a meeting for which a permission under subsection (2) is in effect may all participate by a means of communication referred to in that subsection.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33B(4) (src:697)
GIVEN `section 33B applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      means IS A `Means of participating in a meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`all the members may participate by this means` `section 33B applies` `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` means MEANS
    `section 33B applies` AND `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect`

-- src:698 | (5) A meeting for which a permission under subsection (2) is in effect may be held at 2 or more places at the same time.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 33B(5) (src:698)
GIVEN `section 33B applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of places at which the meeting is held at the same time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the meeting may be held at that number of places at the same time` `section 33B applies` `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect` `the number of places at which the meeting is held at the same time` MEANS
    IF   `section 33B applies` AND `a permission under subsection 33B(2) is in effect`
         AND `the number of places at which the meeting is held at the same time` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Sections 34 and 34AAA: hearing and determining a matter; holders of offices`

DECLARE `Source of authority to hear and determine a matter` IS ONE OF
    `authority given by law`
    `authority given by consent of the parties`
    `no authority to hear and determine the matter`

DECLARE `Thing done at a hearing` IS ONE OF
    `to receive evidence`
    `to examine witnesses`
    `to administer an oath or affirmation to a witness`
    `to do something else at the hearing`

-- "Any court, Judge, justice of the peace, officer, commissioner, arbitrator, or other person" is a list that ends in "other person", so the
-- kind of person makes no difference: what matters is the authority to hear and determine the matter, by law or by consent (fork F23).
-- src:699 | 34 Power to hear and determine a matter includes power to receive evidence and examine witnesses etc.
-- src:700 | Any court, Judge, justice of the peace, officer, commissioner, arbitrator, or other person authorised by law, or by consent of parties, to hear and determine any matter, shall have authority to receive evidence and examine witnesses and to administer an oath or affirmation to all witnesses legally called before them respectively.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34 (src:699-700)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of authority to hear and determine a matter`
      thing IS A `Thing done at a hearing`
      `the witness is legally called before the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person authorised to hear and determine the matter has authority to do this` source thing `the witness is legally called before the person` MEANS
    IF source EQUALS `no authority to hear and determine the matter`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `to receive evidence` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to examine witnesses` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `to administer an oath or affirmation to a witness` THEN `the witness is legally called before the person`
         WHEN `to do something else at the hearing` THEN FALSE

-- src:701 | 34AAA Exercise of powers etc. by holders etc. of offices or positions
-- src:702 | If an Act confers a power or function or imposes a duty on a person holding or occupying an office or position as such, then the power may be exercised or the function or duty must be performed by the person for the time being holding or occupying the office or position.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAA (src:701-702)
GIVEN `the Act confers the power, function or duty on a person holding or occupying an office or position as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person for the time being holding or occupying the office or position` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the person who exercises the power or performs the function or duty` `the Act confers the power, function or duty on a person holding or occupying an office or position as such` `the person for the time being holding or occupying the office or position` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers the power, function or duty on a person holding or occupying an office or position as such`
    THEN JUST `the person for the time being holding or occupying the office or position`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 34AAB: a Minister may authorise others to act on his or her behalf`

DECLARE `Person a Minister may authorise` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister who does not administer the Act or provision`
    `a member of the Executive Council who is not a Minister`
    `a Minister who administers the Act or provision`
    `any other person`

DECLARE `Source of a function, duty or power` IS ONE OF
    `the Act or provision`
    `an instrument having effect under or for the purposes of the Act or provision`
    `a source outside the Act or provision and its instruments`

DECLARE `Way an authorisation is expressed` IS ONE OF
    `to have effect only during a period or periods`
    `to have effect only during the existence of a circumstance or circumstances`
    `to take effect immediately and afterwards continue until another person is appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister`
    `to take effect at a time referred to in the authorisation and afterwards continue until another person is appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister`
    `to be expressed in some other way`

DECLARE `Authorisation or revocation` IS ONE OF
    `an authorisation under subsection 34AAB(1)`
    `the revocation of such an authorisation`
    `something that is neither`

-- src:704 | (1) A Minister (the authorising Minister) who administers (whether alone or jointly with one or more other Ministers) an Act or a provision of an Act may authorise:
-- src:705 | (a) a Minister who does not administer the Act or provision; or
-- src:706 | (b) a member of the Executive Council who is not a Minister;
-- src:707 | to act on behalf of the authorising Minister in the performance of functions or duties, or the exercise of powers, that the authorising Minister may perform or exercise under the Act or provision.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(1) (src:704-707)
GIVEN `the authorising Minister administers the Act or provision, alone or jointly with one or more other Ministers` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person a Minister may authorise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may authorise this person to act on the Minister's behalf` `the authorising Minister administers the Act or provision, alone or jointly with one or more other Ministers` person MEANS
    `the authorising Minister administers the Act or provision, alone or jointly with one or more other Ministers`
    AND (person EQUALS `a Minister who does not administer the Act or provision` OR person EQUALS `a member of the Executive Council who is not a Minister`)

-- src:708 | (2) An authorisation under subsection (1) in relation to an Act or a provision of an Act extends to the performance of functions or duties, or the exercise of powers, that the authorising Minister may perform or exercise under an instrument (including a regulation, rule or Proclamation) having effect under or for the purposes of the Act or provision.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(2) (src:708)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of a function, duty or power`
      `the authorising Minister may perform or exercise it under that source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the authorisation extends to the function, duty or power` source `the authorising Minister may perform or exercise it under that source` MEANS
    `the authorising Minister may perform or exercise it under that source` AND (NOT (source EQUALS `a source outside the Act or provision and its instruments`))

-- src:709 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), an authorisation under subsection (1) may be expressed:
-- src:710 | (a) to have effect only during a period or periods, or during the existence of a circumstance or circumstances, referred to in the authorisation; or
-- src:711 | (b) to take effect immediately, or at a time referred to in the authorisation, and afterwards to continue to have effect until another person is appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(3) (src:709-711)
GIVEN way IS A `Way an authorisation is expressed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an authorisation may be expressed in this way` way MEANS
    NOT (way EQUALS `to be expressed in some other way`)

-- src:711 | (b) to take effect immediately, or at a time referred to in the authorisation, and afterwards to continue to have effect until another person is appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister.
-- src:712 | (4) An authorisation under subsection (1) may be revoked at any time by the authorising Minister.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(3)(b) and (4) (src:711-712)
GIVEN `the authorisation was expressed in a way referred to in paragraph 34AAB(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person has been appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorising Minister has revoked it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the authorisation continues to have effect` `the authorisation was expressed in a way referred to in paragraph 34AAB(3)(b)` `another person has been appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister` `the authorising Minister has revoked it` MEANS
    `the authorisation was expressed in a way referred to in paragraph 34AAB(3)(b)`
    AND (NOT `another person has been appointed to the office held by the authorising Minister`)
    AND (NOT `the authorising Minister has revoked it`)

-- src:712 | (4) An authorisation under subsection (1) may be revoked at any time by the authorising Minister.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(4) (src:712)
GIVEN `the authorisation was given under subsection 34AAB(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person revoking it is the authorising Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the authorisation may be revoked at any time` `the authorisation was given under subsection 34AAB(1)` `the person revoking it is the authorising Minister` MEANS
    `the authorisation was given under subsection 34AAB(1)` AND `the person revoking it is the authorising Minister`

-- src:713 | (5) An authorisation under subsection (1), and the revocation of such an authorisation, must be in writing.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(5) (src:713)
GIVEN thing IS A `Authorisation or revocation`
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it complies with subsection 34AAB(5)` thing `it is in writing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an authorisation under subsection 34AAB(1)` THEN JUST `it is in writing`
    WHEN `the revocation of such an authorisation` THEN JUST `it is in writing`
    WHEN `something that is neither` THEN NOTHING

-- src:714 | (6) This section does not affect the giving, under a power existing apart from this section, of an authorisation to a Minister or other member of the Executive Council to act on behalf of another Minister.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AAB(6) (src:714)
GIVEN `a power exists apart from section 34AAB to authorise a Minister or other member of the Executive Council to act on behalf of another Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 34AAB stops the giving of an authorisation under that other power` `a power exists apart from section 34AAB to authorise a Minister or other member of the Executive Council to act on behalf of another Minister` MEANS
    IF `a power exists apart from section 34AAB to authorise a Minister or other member of the Executive Council to act on behalf of another Minister`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Sections 34AA and 34AB: delegation`

DECLARE `How a delegate is described` IS ONE OF
    `a specified person`
    `any person from time to time holding the specified office or position`
    `any person from time to time occupying the specified office or position`
    `any person from time to time performing the duties of the specified office or position`
    `some other description of a delegate`

DECLARE `Way a delegation may be made` IS ONE OF
    `the delegation is made generally`
    `the delegation is made as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation`
    `the delegation is made in some other way`

-- src:715 | 34AA Delegation to persons holding, occupying or performing the duties of an office or position
-- src:716 | Where an Act confers power to delegate a function, duty or power, then the power of delegation shall not be construed as being limited to delegating the function, duty or power to a specified person but shall be construed as including a power to delegate the function, duty or power to any person from time to time holding, occupying, or performing the duties of, a specified office or position, even if the office or position does not come into existence until after the delegation is given.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AA (src:715-716)
GIVEN `the Act confers power to delegate a function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      described IS A `How a delegate is described`
      `the office or position does not come into existence until after the delegation is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power of delegation includes delegating to a delegate described in this way` `the Act confers power to delegate a function, duty or power` described `the office or position does not come into existence until after the delegation is given` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers power to delegate a function, duty or power`
    THEN CONSIDER described
         WHEN `a specified person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `any person from time to time holding the specified office or position` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `any person from time to time occupying the specified office or position` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `any person from time to time performing the duties of the specified office or position` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `some other description of a delegate` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:719 | (1) Where an Act confers power on a person or body (in this section called the authority) to delegate a function, duty or power:
-- src:720 | (a) the delegation may be made either generally or as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(1)(a) (src:719-720)
GIVEN `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way a delegation may be made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegation may be made in this way` `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` way MEANS
    IF `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power`
    THEN CONSIDER way
         WHEN `the delegation is made generally` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the delegation is made as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the delegation is made in some other way` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:719 | (1) Where an Act confers power on a person or body (in this section called the authority) to delegate a function, duty or power:
-- src:721 | (b) the powers that may be delegated do not include that power to delegate;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(1)(b) (src:719-721)
GIVEN `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the power to delegate is among the powers that may be delegated` `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:719 | (1) Where an Act confers power on a person or body (in this section called the authority) to delegate a function, duty or power:
-- src:722 | (c) a function, duty or power so delegated, when performed or exercised by the delegate, shall, for the purposes of the Act, be deemed to have been performed or exercised by the authority;
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(1)(c) (src:719-722)
GIVEN `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate performed or exercised the function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`for the purposes of the Act it is deemed to have been performed or exercised by the authority` `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` `the delegate performed or exercised the function, duty or power` MEANS
    `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` AND `the delegate performed or exercised the function, duty or power`

-- src:719 | (1) Where an Act confers power on a person or body (in this section called the authority) to delegate a function, duty or power:
-- src:723 | (d) a delegation by the authority does not prevent the performance or exercise of a function, duty or power by the authority; and
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(1)(d) (src:719-723)
GIVEN `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has delegated the function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegation prevents the authority from performing or exercising the function, duty or power` `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` `the authority has delegated the function, duty or power` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` AND `the authority has delegated the function, duty or power`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:719 | (1) Where an Act confers power on a person or body (in this section called the authority) to delegate a function, duty or power:
-- src:724 | (e) if the authority is not a person, section 34A applies as if it were.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(1)(e) (src:719-724)
GIVEN `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34A applies to the authority as if it were a person` `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` `the authority is a person` MEANS
    `the Act confers power on a person or body to delegate a function, duty or power` AND (NOT `the authority is a person`)

-- 34AB(2): "on and after the amendment taking effect" includes the day it takes effect.
-- src:726 | (2) If:
-- src:727 | (a) a person (the delegator) or body (also the delegator) delegates all the person’s or body’s functions, duties or powers under an Act, or a provision of an Act, to another person or body; and
-- src:728 | (b) the Act is amended to give the delegator one or more additional functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision; and
-- src:729 | (c) the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect;
-- src:730 | then, on and after the amendment taking effect, the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(2) (src:726-730)
GIVEN `the delegator delegates all of its functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision to another person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act is amended to give the delegator one or more additional functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the amendment takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegation is taken to include the additional functions, duties or powers on this day` `the delegator delegates all of its functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision to another person or body` `the Act is amended to give the delegator one or more additional functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision` `the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect` `the day the amendment takes effect` `the day in question` MEANS
        `the delegator delegates all of its functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision to another person or body`
    AND `the Act is amended to give the delegator one or more additional functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision`
    AND `the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect`
    AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day the amendment takes effect`

-- src:732 | (3) If:
-- src:733 | (a) a person or body delegates one or more of the person’s or body’s functions, duties or powers under an Act, or a provision of an Act, to another person or body; and
-- src:734 | (b) the Act is amended to alter the scope of one or more of those functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision; and
-- src:735 | (c) the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect;
-- src:736 | then, on and after the amendment taking effect, the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34AB(3) (src:732-736)
GIVEN `the delegator delegates one or more of its functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision to another person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act is amended to alter the scope of one or more of those functions, duties or powers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the amendment takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the delegation is taken to include the functions, duties or powers as altered on this day` `the delegator delegates one or more of its functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision to another person or body` `the Act is amended to alter the scope of one or more of those functions, duties or powers` `the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect` `the day the amendment takes effect` `the day in question` MEANS
        `the delegator delegates one or more of its functions, duties or powers under the Act or provision to another person or body`
    AND `the Act is amended to alter the scope of one or more of those functions, duties or powers`
    AND `the delegation is in force immediately before the amendment takes effect`
    AND `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day the amendment takes effect`

§§ `Section 34B(1A): deemed presentation of a paper`

-- 34B(2), the meaning of paper, is in the table of meanings in au-part2-terms.l4. 34B(1) is in au-part7-powers.l4.
-- src:747 | (1A) For the purposes of an Act or a law of a Territory that refers to papers presented (however the presentation is described) to the Parliament or to both Houses, or to each or either House, of the Parliament:
-- src:748 | (а) presentation of a paper in a House of the Parliament in accordance with the rules or orders of the House; or
-- src:749 | (b) if, under the rules or orders of a House of the Parliament, papers are to be deemed to be presented to the House if they are delivered to the Clerk of the House and recorded in the records of the proceedings of the House—such a delivery and recording of a paper;
-- src:750 | shall be deemed to have been presentation of the paper to that House, as described in that Act or law, effected or caused by the person who so presented or delivered the paper or caused the paper to be so presented or delivered.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34B(1A) (src:747-750)
GIVEN `the Act or law refers to papers presented to the Parliament, to both Houses, or to each or either House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paper is presented in the House in accordance with the rules or orders of the House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the rules or orders of the House, papers are deemed to be presented if they are delivered to the Clerk and recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paper is so delivered and recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the paper is deemed to have been presented to the House as the Act or law describes` `the Act or law refers to papers presented to the Parliament, to both Houses, or to each or either House` `the paper is presented in the House in accordance with the rules or orders of the House` `under the rules or orders of the House, papers are deemed to be presented if they are delivered to the Clerk and recorded` `the paper is so delivered and recorded` MEANS
        `the Act or law refers to papers presented to the Parliament, to both Houses, or to each or either House`
    AND (   `the paper is presented in the House in accordance with the rules or orders of the House`
         OR (`under the rules or orders of the House, papers are deemed to be presented if they are delivered to the Clerk and recorded` AND `the paper is so delivered and recorded`))

-- src:750 | shall be deemed to have been presentation of the paper to that House, as described in that Act or law, effected or caused by the person who so presented or delivered the paper or caused the paper to be so presented or delivered.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34B(1A) (src:750)
GIVEN `the paper is deemed to have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who presented or delivered the paper, or caused it to be so presented or delivered` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the person by whom the presentation is deemed to have been effected or caused` `the paper is deemed to have been presented` `the person who presented or delivered the paper, or caused it to be so presented or delivered` MEANS
    IF `the paper is deemed to have been presented`
    THEN JUST `the person who presented or delivered the paper, or caused it to be so presented or delivered`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 34C(5) and (6)(b): the extension of a periodic report`

-- src:765 | (5) A Minister may, on application under subsection (4), grant such extension as he or she considers reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(5) (src:765)
GIVEN `an application was made under subsection 34C(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister considers the extension reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may grant the extension` `an application was made under subsection 34C(4)` `the Minister considers the extension reasonable in the circumstances` MEANS
    `an application was made under subsection 34C(4)` AND `the Minister considers the extension reasonable in the circumstances`

-- 34C(6)(b): the period as extended runs from the first day of the specified period to the extended last day. The same test as 34C(4)
-- is applied, with the extended last day as the end.
-- src:768 | (b) the person who made the application shall furnish the periodic report to the Minister within the period as so extended; and
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 34C(6)(b) (src:768)
GIVEN `a Minister granted an extension on an application under subsection 34C(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person furnishes the report` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the specified period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period as extended` IS A DATE
      closures IS A `Days of closure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person furnishes the report within the period as extended` `a Minister granted an extension on an application under subsection 34C(4)` `the day the person furnishes the report` `the first day of the specified period` `the last day of the period as extended` closures MEANS
    `a Minister granted an extension on an application under subsection 34C(4)`
    AND `the thing is done within the time allowed` `the day the person furnishes the report` `the first day of the specified period` `the last day of the period as extended` closures
